
. * generated by run_all.py: the package root is the first argument
. args root

. global PKGROOT `"`root'"'

. cd `"`root'/02_code/10_analysis"'
<PACKAGE_ROOT>/02_code/10_analysis

. do "A2_5.do" corrected2x 

. /****************************************************************************
> ***
>  A2_5.do -- item A2.5 moderator interactions on own and identical observation
> s (R1.4, R2.5)
>  Moderators (mod): cd    = cul_dist (package Hofstede cd6_ge4; Table 5)
>                    cdnp  = cul_dist on pairs without any regional proxy (any_
> regional_proxy==0)
>                    cdoff = cd_off, rebuilt from the official 2015-08-16 workb
> ook only (A2_00_hofstede.py)
>                    col   = comlang_off (Table 5 language moderator)
>                    eth   = comlang_ethno (CEPII Gravity)
>                    csl   = Melitz-Toubal common spoken language (CEPII Langua
> ge, ling_web.dta)
>                    cnl   = Melitz-Toubal common native language
>  Model (CORE 07_table5_moderators.do:11-43): ppmlhdfe v_ttl_k mob  mob*(M - c
> ), FE as baseline,
>  directed-pair clusters. Two centrings for EVERY model (audit check):
>    orig     = Table 5 rule: cd types centred on the ELIGIBLE sample mean befo
> re ppmlhdfe drops
>               (07_table5:14-16 "summarize cul_dist if !missing(v_ttl_k, mob_b
> ilat_vis, cul_dist)");
>               language types uncentred (07_table5:11-12), so the main slope i
> s the slope at M = 0.
>    realized = centred on the mean of M over the realized e(sample); re-estima
> ted, e(sample)
>               asserted unchanged (iterated if it changed).
>  The interaction coefficient must be invariant to the centring (asserted, 1e-
> 6 relative); only
>  the main slope moves. Common visitor-tourist sample: rows retained in both o
> wn (orig) models,
>  then the fixed point of both refits; there "orig" keeps each measure's own T
> able 5 constant and
>  "realized" uses the common-sample mean for both measures (the stacked tests 
> use the latter).
>  Help: ppmlhdfe.sthlp, [R] lincom, [R] test, [R] summarize (detail percentile
> s), [R] centile.
> *****************************************************************************
> **/
. args vintage

. clear all

. set more off

. set varabbrev off

. set linesize 200

. version 18.0

. do "00_config.do" `vintage'

. /*******************************************************************************
>  00_config.do  --  globals for one data vintage (analysis layer of the replication package)
> 
>  Usage (from another do-file, cwd = 02_code/10_analysis):  do 00_config.do <vintage>
>    <vintage> = corrected2x (revised baseline, default run)
>              | corrected | corrected2 (reconciliation switch, same data build)
>              | submitted (reconciliation switch, needs a second build with corrections off)
>  Every path is built from the package root ${PKGROOT}, which run_all.py passes as the first
>  argument of the generated wrapper do-file (_run.do pattern); nothing here is machine-specific.
>  Defines globals only and checks the Stata version.
> 
>  Vintages (see README.md, "Data-correction rules"):
>    corrected   = build with the correction rules on (code 490 -> TWN, Paraguay residence quarantine, flags)
>    corrected2  = corrected + quarantine of PAK residence 2020-2021 and BLR visitors-by-residence
>                  partner LIE 2020-2022 (same rule as Paraguay); 31-code outcome
>    corrected2x = corrected2 with the 30-code outcome (31-code basket minus HS 490700) = revised baseline
>    submitted   = original data as submitted (build with corrections off), for the reconciliation only
> *******************************************************************************/
. 
. args vintage

. if !inlist("`vintage'", "submitted", "corrected", "corrected2", "corrected2x") {
.     display as error "VINTAGE must be submitted, corrected, corrected2 or corrected2x; got [`vintage']"
.     exit 198
. }

. 
. version 18.0

. if c(stata_version) < 18 {
.     display as error "Stata 18 or newer required; running " c(stata_version)
.     exit 9
. }

. 
. global VINTAGE "`vintage'"

